# The round constants of SHA-256 and of MD5, each a word of 32 bits held in
# an `i64` from 0 to 2^32 - 1. SHA-256's are the first 32 bits of the
# fractional parts of the cube roots of the first 64 primes (FIPS 180-4,
# 4.2.2), computed with whole numbers alone; MD5's are the integer parts of
# 2^32 times the sine of 1 to 64 in radians (RFC 1321, 3.4). The tests of
# `crypto/internal/sha256` and `crypto/internal/md5` hold them to the
# standards' own test vectors.

